Hello 3Dnatives team,

a pitch with a detail that may matter for your multilingual editions:
Solidon3D ships its interface and its complete manual in six languages,
German, English, Spanish, French, Italian and Portuguese. Not a machine
translation of the menus, but the manual as well.

The product is a desktop application that sits between a downloaded 3D model
and the slicer. Click a hole and its dimensions appear on the model itself,
type 8 instead of 6 and the countersink follows, pick a fit for the screw,
read the check report before you export, hand the file to the slicer you
already use. No CAD knowledge required.

That fills a gap that has been open for years. CAD packages accept an STL but
their tools cannot grip triangles, so the part gets rebuilt. The mesh tools
that could edit them are discontinued, Meshmixer and Microsoft's 3D Builder.
Parametric customisers only work when the original author anticipated the
parameter.

Version 0.5.0 is the largest step so far. Until now the result of an edit was
a triangle mesh; now it is an exact body. Holes, countersinks and threads stay
exact when they are moved, duplicated or removed, and STEP goes in and comes
back out cleanly. Two geometry kernels run under one interface and the options
that used to switch between them are gone; the software keeps the exact body
where it can and names the limit where it cannot.

The most visual addition: a honeycomb pattern, knurl or set of ribs is
recognised as one feature with pitch, cell width and depth instead of hundreds
of faces. One click removes it, three numbers set it again, including around a
handle, where the pattern is measured in the unrolled surface so the grooves
are equally deep and the circumference closes without a seam.

Also worth a line: clearance is entered as a reference to the material rather
than as a number, and the material profiles can be calibrated to a specific
printer from printed test pieces. Change the material and every fit in the
project follows.

The demo is free and complete, so anything above can be checked directly.
Print-resolution images are available on request.

Solidon3D is an independent development from Germany, for Windows, macOS and
Linux, fully usable offline after a single activation, with no account and no
telemetry.

